{%- comment -%}
  Guido on the PC, introduced once at the foot of the page.

  There is no second product any more: the same Guido runs on a Windows PC, and
  this section is the only place that is explained and the only place its
  download link lives. The "Get started" tabs for Le Mans Ultimate and the
  Assetto Corsa games link down here.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- comment -%}
  Pinned to the release that carries Assetto Corsa EVO. Do not deploy this page before that MSI exists at the
  URL: the download button is the only way most people get Guido on the PC, and a 404 here reads as "the
  product is broken" rather than "the release slipped".
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign desktop_download_url = 'https://releases.matto.club/guido/v1.4.0/guido-1.4.0.msi' -%}
<section class="product-desktop" id="desktop">
  <h2 class="product-section-title">Guido on the PC</h2>
  <div class="product-desktop-body">
    <p>
      Guido runs on the PC as well as on your phone: the same app, the same dashboard, one installer. It sits in
      the tray alongside your sim titles, reads their telemetry and carries it over your home network.
    </p>
    <p>
      It runs with no window, starts itself when you log on, and streams telemetry from any active session. No
      setup needed, no messing with your sim, no asking for admin rights. It is built with a minimal footprint,
      so it does not interfere with your sim's performance.
    </p>
    <p>
      It is how Guido reaches Le Mans Ultimate and the Assetto Corsa games: Assetto Corsa, Assetto Corsa
      Competizione and Assetto Corsa EVO. Gran Turismo 7 talks to Guido directly instead, and does not need it.
    </p>
    <div class="product-desktop-download">
      {%- comment -%}
        The platform rides inside the button rather than on a line beside it, so
        the label says what you get and where it runs in one read.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <a class="ds-btn ds-btn--primary" href="{{ desktop_download_url }}">
        {% svg 'icons/windows.svg' %} Download Guido for Windows
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
